# data file for the Fltk User Interface Designer (fluid)
version 1.0500
header_name {.h}
code_name {.cxx}
comment {Reusable "drop files here" panel: a count label, a tree of loaded files,
add/clear buttons, and an invisible drag-and-drop overlay sitting on top of
the tree.

Place it in another .fl with an Fl_Group node whose class is FileLoadPanel,
plus a global decl including this header. Behaviour is attached from Haskell
by Onyx.GUI.Core.fileLoadPanel.

The labels here are plain English placeholders so the editor stays readable.
They are not {keys}: each host tab supplies its own wording from a different
Fluent message, so Haskell overwrites all three at wire-up time.

The tree is the resizable child, so hosts can place this at any size and the
label and buttons keep their heights while the tree absorbs the slack.

Designed at 900x525, the size a Misc tab places it at, so that the common
case needs no scaling at all. Fl_Group::resize scales proportionally, which
would otherwise widen the gap between the two buttons along with everything
else; at other sizes that is what happens, and it is only cosmetic.} {in_source not_in_header
}

decl {\#include "hs_tree.h"} {public global
}

decl {\#include "hs_dnd_box.h"} {public global
}

widget_class FileLoadPanel {open
  xywh {0 0 900 525} box FLAT_BOX
} {
  Fl_Box countLabel {
    label {0 files}
    xywh {10 10 880 25}
  }
  Fl_Tree tree {
    xywh {10 45 880 425} resizable
    class HsTree
  }
  Fl_Button addButton {
    label Add
    xywh {10 480 435 35}
  }
  Fl_Button clearButton {
    label Clear
    xywh {455 480 435 35}
  }
  Fl_Box dndOverlay {
    xywh {10 45 880 425}
    class HsDndBox
  }
  code {// FLUID builds the children at their design coordinates, which assume this
// group sits at the origin at its design size. Restate that, then resize
// into the frame we were actually constructed with, so that Fl_Group::resize
// maps the children across. Keep the numbers below in step with the xywh of
// the widget_class itself.
Fl_Widget::resize(0, 0, 900, 525);
resize(X, Y, W, H);} {}
}
